## Develop

Open the repository in its devcontainer, which has Go 1.26 and golangci-lint.

```sh
go run . --help      # run it
go test ./...        # test it
{{- if .Standard }}
make check           # what CI runs: tidy, format, vet, lint, test with -race
make build           # bin/{{ .Container }}, versioned with git describe
make dist            # release binaries for Linux, macOS and Windows in dist/
make help            # every target
{{- else }}
go build -o bin/{{ .Container }} .
{{- end }}
```

`{{ .Container }} --version` prints the version the binary was built with: the
`-ldflags "-X main.version=..."` of the build, or `dev`.

## Layout

- `main.go` is the command: it parses the command line and calls into
  `internal/`. Its `run` function returns the exit code instead of exiting, so
  `main_test.go` tests the whole program.
- `internal/` holds the packages, one purpose each; `internal/doc.go` explains
  the rules.
- Tests sit next to the code; fixtures and golden files in `testdata/`.
